  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text, \"The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to rename or move a committed requirement only with the user's agreement, using `habeas-refactor`, and to commit the rename or move before changing the requirement's text\", states what the skill's content says. It prescribes no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or delegation interface for building anything. The one named tool, `habeas-refactor`, is the thing the skill must tell agents to use. A skill document that gave the same direction in different words or a different place would still satisfy the text. So no clause is structural, and no implementation root is needed for one.\n\nThe supplied root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` does contain the direction. In `section[Habeas requirements]/section[Workflow]/paragraph@6029f1f0972d` it says: \"Renaming or moving a committed requirement is a habeas-refactor task, agreed with the user and committed before its text changes.\" That covers all three parts: the user's agreement, `habeas-refactor`, and committing before the text changes. The front matter description also sends moves of requirements to `habeas-refactor`. Checking that the content matches the text is behavioral, so I left it to the behavioral criterion.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement says the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to do three things when renaming or moving a committed requirement. They must use `habeas-refactor`, do it only with the user's agreement, and commit the change before the text changes. These are all obligations about the bundled skill's content.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_renames_requirements_through_refactor_before_editing]` carries the `{test}` marker. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`, which runs `assert_text` over `bundled_skill(\"habeas-requirements\")`. `bundled_skill` joins `SKILL.md` and its reference files and collapses whitespace. `assert_text` asserts that the text contains the phrase. The phrase is \"Renaming or moving a committed requirement is a habeas-refactor task, agreed with the user and committed before its text changes\".\n\nThe phrase covers each obligation:\n- **Which changes:** \"Renaming or moving a committed requirement\".\n- **Using `habeas-refactor`:** \"is a habeas-refactor task\".\n- **User's agreement:** \"agreed with the user\".\n- **Commit before the text changes:** \"committed before its text changes\".\n\nThe skill file `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, under Workflow, contains this sentence. It wraps across lines in the source, and the whitespace collapse makes the match work. If the sentence were removed or changed, the assertion would fail.\n\nThe requirement has no other behavioral obligations, so no gap remains.",
